cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Local AI Control Center
message: >-
  If you use this software in work that gets published, please cite it
  using the metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alejandro
    family-names: Segura
    alias: asegura-dev
repository-code: "https://github.com/asegura-dev/local-ai-control-center"
abstract: >-
  A local-first Python framework for AI-assisted work on your own
  documents, built for research that cannot be sent to a hosted service.
  Capabilities are off by default and configuration is a ceiling that
  removes rather than grants; every path is checked against a workspace
  boundary; every run is previewed and confirmed before it acts, and
  recorded in a hash-chained audit trail. Quotations returned by a model
  are checked against the source document they claim to come from, so a
  fabricated citation is reported rather than presented as fact. The
  engine runs locally, or on another machine the user owns and names in
  their configuration. It is a control layer, not an autonomous agent.
keywords:
  - local-first
  - reproducible-research
  - large-language-models
  - provenance
  - audit-trail
  - citation-verification
  - human-in-the-loop
  - ollama
license: MIT
version: 0.35.0
date-released: "2026-09-10"
